<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (John Sullivan Dwight)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1855</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English adaptation, freer than a translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Organ arrangement</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1855</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Night Divine (Hart Pease Danks)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">late 19th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English adaptation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Violin performance on radio (Reginald Fessenden)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1906</span><span class="sg-chain-h">performance, often called the first song broadcast</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Mariah Carey)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1994</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (John Berry)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Medley with O Come, All Ye Faithful (Trans-Siberian Orchestra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Martina McBride)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1997</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Celine Dion)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1998</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Josh Groban)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Josh Gracin)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2006</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Glee cast)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2010</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Ladywell Primary School, Motherwell)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">charity recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Holy Night (Lauren Daigle)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2017</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li></ul></section>
